t;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-1-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-2-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-3-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-2-0&quot;], &quot;coreq-immediate&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-0-0&quot;], &quot;postcoreq&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-0-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-2-0&quot;]}, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-2-0&quot;: {&quot;prereq-immediate&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-3-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-4-0&quot;], &quot;prereq-sequence&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-1-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-2-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-2-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-3-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-2-0&quot;], &quot;coreq-immediate&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-0-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-1-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-3-0&quot;], &quot;postcoreq&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-3-0&quot;]}, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-3-0&quot;: {&quot;prereq-immediate&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-3-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-4-0&quot;], &quot;prereq-sequence&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-1-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-2-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-2-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-3-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-2-0&quot;], &quot;coreq-immediate&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-2-0&quot;], &quot;coreq-sequence&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-0-0&quot;, &quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-1-0&quot;], &quot;postcoreq&quot;: [&quot;nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-2-0&quot;]}}\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">Scroll right for more semesters \u2192</div><div class=\"flow-scroll\"><div class=\"flow-container\">\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-summer\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 1</span><span class=\"col-term\">Summer</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Science of Professional Nursing Practice&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This foundational nursing course enables students to develop an understanding of the science of professional nursing using the Scope and Standards of Nursing Practice and Code of Ethics as a framework for the professional nursing role. Students are introduced to the role of the nurse in interprofessional collaborative practice that promotes wellness, manages illness and achieves quality and safety outcomes. Through the application and understanding of critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and predictive management, students are prepared to become situational thinkers to provide evidence-based, culturally relevant, patient-centered care across the lifespan.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;5&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: Admission to Nursing program and Co-Req NSG 313 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 312LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Science of Professional Nursing Practice</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">5 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Health Promotion and Disease Prevention in Professional Nursing Practice Across the Lifespan&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course focuses on health promotion and disease prevention for individuals and families. Students will apply the nursing process to promote holistic health across the lifespan using evidence to critically examine and identify influences on health and well-being. Students will analyze national health indicators, situational and contextual issues that impact wellness and group functioning that serve as a basis for identifying the needs and disparities in health and wellness.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: Admission to Nursing program.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 310LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Health Promotion and Disease Prevention in Professional Nursing Practice Across the Lifespan</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-0-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Application of Healthcare Informatics to Promote Health, Quality and Safety&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course builds upon communication literacy concepts through application of computer and information technology that impacts nursing practice. The use of information management systems is explored in relationship to interprofessional communication, management of data to inform knowledge, prevent and mitigate error, and support decision-making. Emphasis is placed on monitoring trends in practice and in outcomes of care. Students are introduced to research and evidence-based practice standards in information systems to improve cost-effectiveness, safety, and quality.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: Admission to the Nursing program.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 314LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Application of Healthcare Informatics to Promote Health, Quality and Safety</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(12 weeks; may also be completed in a different semester shown)</div></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">14 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-summer\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 1</span><span class=\"col-term\">Summer</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Wellness and Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities I&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course promotes wellness and a healthier lifestyle for individuals, families and populations, across the wellness-illness continuum. Selected concepts and exemplars provide a foundation for the development of conceptual thinking and skills to facilitate clinical reasoning. Through the application and understanding of critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and predictive management, students will use situational thinking to provide evidence-based, culturally relevant, patient-centered collaborative care across the lifespan.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;5&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: NSG 310 , NSG 312 , NSG 313 , NSG 314 ; Co-Req NSG 317&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 316LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Wellness and Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities I</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">5 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Wellness &amp; Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities I - Practicum&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;The practicum provides an opportunity to promote wellness and a healthier lifestyle for individuals, families and populations, across the wellness-illness continuum. Students will apply critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and predictive management; using situational thinking to provide evidence-based, culturally relevant, patient-centered collaborative care across the lifespan in clinical settings.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Pass/Not Pass (PNP)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: NSG 310 , NSG 312 , NSG 313 , NSG 314 ; Co-Req NSG 316&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 317LAB</span><span class=\"box-title\">Wellness &amp; Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities I - Practicum</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Social Determinants and Justice in Local and Global Settings&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course examines the cultural, political, economic, educational, environmental and health systems that impact healthcare in local, regional and global populations. Concepts of public health, epidemiology and community assessment will support a primary prevention and wellness focus. The value of relationships and collaborative practice for understanding and addressing community-identified needs, increasing inclusivity and diversity, and for strengthening community assets will be explored. Students will advocate for populations using health promotion, educational, and community empowerment strategies.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: NSG 310 and NSG 314&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 315LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Social Determinants and Justice in Local and Global Settings</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-1-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Application of Healthcare Informatics to Promote Health, Quality and Safety&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course builds upon communication literacy concepts through application of computer and information technology that impacts nursing practice. The use of information management systems is explored in relationship to interprofessional communication, management of data to inform knowledge, prevent and mitigate error, and support decision-making. Emphasis is placed on monitoring trends in practice and in outcomes of care. Students are introduced to research and evidence-based practice standards in information systems to improve cost-effectiveness, safety, and quality.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisites: Admission to the Nursing program.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 314LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Application of Healthcare Informatics to Promote Health, Quality and Safety</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(12 weeks continued; may also be completed in a different semester shown)</div></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">12 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Wellness and Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities II&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course builds on the foundation of Wellness and Illness I, expanding student?s abilities to promote wellness and a healthier lifestyle for individuals, families and populations, across the wellness-illness continuum. Selected concepts and exemplars provide for further development of conceptual thinking and skills to facilitate clinical reasoning. Through the application and understanding of critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and predictive management, students will continue to broaden their situational thinking abilities to provide evidence-based, culturally relevant, patient-centered collaborative care across the lifespan.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;5&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 315 and NSG 316 and NSG 317 and NSG 348 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 412 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 411LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Wellness and Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities II</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">5 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Wellness &amp; Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families, and Communities II - Practicum&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course builds on the foundation of Wellness and Illness I Practicum, providing an opportunity to promote wellness and a healthier lifestyle for individuals, families and populations, across the wellness-illness continuum in varying health care settings. Students will apply critical thinking, clinical reasoning, and predictive management; using situational thinking to provide evidence-based, culturally relevant, patient-centered collaborative care across the lifespan in professional practice.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Pass/Not Pass (PNP)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 315 and NSG 316 and NSG 317 and NSG 348 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 411 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 412LAB</span><span class=\"box-title\">Wellness &amp; Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families, and Communities II - Practicum</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Evidence Based Practice and Nursing Research&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Foundations for evidence-based practice in nursing. Specific elements of evidence-based practice include formulating the clinical question, conducting a search strategy, critically appraising the evidence, and implementation of evidence in the clinical environment. Basic concepts of the research process will form the foundation for assessing the quality of evidence. Explores the relationship between evidence-based findings and nursing practice to achieve favorable and cost-containing client outcomes. Must be taken in program sequence. This course is equivalent to NBC 348 .&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: Sophomore standing. NSG 295 or PSY 207 or STA 119 and STA 119 or SSC 225 or CEP 207 . Completion of Communication Literacy 1 or completion of Writing Skills 1 (ENG 101 or placement into ENG 201); Admission to the Nursing Program.&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 348LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Evidence Based Practice and Nursing Research</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Health Systems Policy and Economics&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course examines the policy and politics involved in the access, cost and quality of healthcare. Students will address economic considerations faced by institutions and key stakeholders. The role of the nurse as a member of the interprofessional team, within the context of the complex healthcare environment, is explored.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 348 and NSG 315 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 413 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 414LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Health Systems Policy and Economics</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-2-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Promoting Quality Health Outcomes in a Culture of Safety&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course examines concepts of quality health outcomes and safety within the context of professional nursing practice. Systems and processes are explored and analyzed to promote and sustain quality health outcomes, and safe, effective healthcare environments. Focus is placed on the role the professional nurse as leader in a collaborative practice in a patient- centered, evidence- based culture of safety.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 315 and NSG 348 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 414 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 413LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Promoting Quality Health Outcomes in a Culture of Safety</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">18 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Wellness and Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities III&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course builds on the foundation of Wellness and Illness I and II, preparing students to transition into professional practice as a member of the interprofessional team. Students will expand their abilities to recognize evolving situations for individuals, families and populations across the lifespan. Focus is placed on synthesizing and analyzing the meaning of assessment findings and relevant data, connecting this information to previous knowledge and experiences to prioritize care and promote quality and safe outcomes.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: null, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 411 and NSG 412 and NSG 413 and NSG 414 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 416 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 415LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Wellness and Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities III</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Wellness &amp; Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities III - Practicum&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course builds on the foundation of Wellness and Illness I and II Practicum, preparing students for the complexities of practice as they transition into professional practice as a member of the interprofessional team. Students will recognize evolving situations for individuals, families and populations across the lifespan. Students will synthesize and analyze assessment findings and relevant trending data, connecting this information to previous knowledge and experiences to prioritize care and promote quality and safe outcomes.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;5&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Pass/Not Pass (PNP)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 411 and NSG 412 and NSG 413 and NSG 414 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 415 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 416LAB</span><span class=\"box-title\">Wellness &amp; Illness Concepts with Individuals, Families and Communities III - Practicum</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">5 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Care Transitions and Care Coordination&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course explores the role of the professional nurse in care coordination to transform healthcare, initiating at the bedside and extending to transition in care. Relationships between health information technology; collaboration; care coordination; and evidence-based, patient-centered care are examined as central forces that impact health outcomes across populations and systems. Focus is placed on developing students? abilities to participate in care management of healthcare consumers in a variety of healthcare settings to maximize their independence and quality of life.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 413 and NSG 414 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 417 and NSG 415 and NSG 416 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 418LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Care Transitions and Care Coordination</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"nursing-bs-accelerated-program__box-3-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Leading Professional Nursing Practice to Achieve Quality Outcomes&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;The purpose of this course is to prepare the baccalaureate nursing student for transition to professional nursing practice as a leader from the bedside to the boardroom. Emphasis is placed on guiding decisions and collaborative practice through the use of ethical decision-making. Students will be prepared to enter practice with the ability to identify, plan, and implement evidence-based strategies to improve quality, safety, and patient outcomes across diverse populations.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Spring&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;Pre-Requisite: NSG 413 and NSG 414 ; Co-Requisite: NSG 418 .&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">NSG 417LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Leading Professional Nursing Practice to Achieve Quality Outcomes</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">59 credits</div>\n      </div></div></div></section>"}